From 63c54f2376c14d9a16482a077465b684ef617e23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel Mac Builds <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 13:05:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] deps: stop macOS frameworks outranking OpenImageIO's pinned
 libraries

OpenImageIO failed to compile against a libtiff header it was never
pointed at:

  tiffoutput.cpp:1288:10: error: no matching function for call to
                                 'TIFFWriteCustomDirectory'
  /Library/Frameworks/Mono.framework/Headers/tiffio.h:413:12: note:
    candidate function not viable: no known conversion from 'uint64_t *'
    to 'uint64 *' for 2nd argument

TIFF_INCLUDE_DIR was correct and pointed at our libtiff 4.7.1. The
header that actually got included came from Mono, which bundles libtiff
4.0.9 -- old enough that TIFFWriteCustomDirectory still took uint64*.

The route in is JPEG. CMAKE_FIND_FRAMEWORK defaults to FIRST on macOS,
so find_package() searches /Library/Frameworks before the paths pinned
here. ZLIB, PNG and TIFF are immune because they are pinned by explicit
_LIBRARY and _INCLUDE_DIR; JPEG is only hinted at through JPEG_ROOT, so
the framework wins and JPEG_INCLUDE_DIR resolves to
/Library/Frameworks/Mono.framework/Headers. That one directory holds
jpeglib.h, png.h and tiffio.h together, and it reaches the compiler as
-isystem ahead of our tiff include -- so an unpinned JPEG quietly
defeats a correctly pinned TIFF.

Set CMAKE_FIND_FRAMEWORK=LAST for this build. It is scoped to APPLE, so
Windows and Linux are untouched, and it fixes the whole class rather
than just the JPEG instance: a self-contained dependency stack should
never prefer a system framework over the libraries it just built.

Only reproducible on hosts with a framework that bundles image
libraries, which is why CI never saw it -- GitHub's runners have no Mono
install. That makes it a portability bug in the build, not a local
quirk: the stack is supposed to be hermetic.
---
 .../build_environment/cmake/openimageio.cmake | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build_files/build_environment/cmake/openimageio.cmake b/build_files/build_environment/cmake/openimageio.cmake
index 2107a9aa..78315ada 100644
--- a/build_files/build_environment/cmake/openimageio.cmake
+++ b/build_files/build_environment/cmake/openimageio.cmake
@@ -107,6 +107,30 @@ set(OPENIMAGEIO_EXTRA_ARGS
   -DLibheif_DIR=${LIBDIR}/libheif/lib/cmake/libheif
 )
 
+if(APPLE)
+  # CMAKE_FIND_FRAMEWORK defaults to FIRST on macOS, so find_package() prefers
+  # anything under /Library/Frameworks over the locations pinned above. ZLIB,
+  # PNG and TIFF survive that because they are pinned by explicit
+  # _LIBRARY/_INCLUDE_DIR; JPEG is only hinted at via JPEG_ROOT, so a stray
+  # framework outranks it. A Mono installation resolves JPEG_INCLUDE_DIR to
+  # /Library/Frameworks/Mono.framework/Headers, and that directory also ships a
+  # libtiff 4.0.9 tiffio.h. It reaches the compiler as -isystem ahead of our
+  # libtiff 4.7.1 and shadows it, so the pinned TIFF is defeated by the
+  # unpinned JPEG:
+  #
+  #   tiffoutput.cpp:1288:10: error: no matching function for call to
+  #                                  'TIFFWriteCustomDirectory'
+  #   Mono.framework/Headers/tiffio.h:413:12: note: candidate not viable: no
+  #                                  known conversion from 'uint64_t *' to 'uint64 *'
+  #
+  # The dependency stack is meant to be self-contained, so make framework
+  # search a last resort rather than the first one.
+  set(OPENIMAGEIO_EXTRA_ARGS
+    ${OPENIMAGEIO_EXTRA_ARGS}
+    -DCMAKE_FIND_FRAMEWORK=LAST
+  )
+endif()
+
 if(WIN32)
   # We don't want the SOABI tags in the final filename since it gets the debug
   # tags wrong and the final .pyd won't be found by python, pybind11 will try to
-- 
